92186311499 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311499 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186310572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311499 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f2f5da27-dc12-5c0e-8352-c31ac3b14b77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311561 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311561 #edb/ref 1069 "q-335265" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311561 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311561 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=7y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=7x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186311561 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0363c023-46f1-587f-a57b-04e2d2812056" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311561 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186311712 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311712 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311712 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311215 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311712 #edb/ref 1069 "q-336481" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311712 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311712 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(0)=c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0)$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the definition of ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ as the standard fundamental matrix by\n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by substitution from lines {{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311712 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9684981a-5306-5edd-b5f3-7d483bf8c5e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311712 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is a fundamental matrix for the system, every solution of the system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c\\,\\text{for some constant vector }c.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{properties of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ By definition, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ satisfies the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nThe second condition here is exactly line $\\text{L4},$ so $\\text{L4}$ follows from the definition of ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ as the standard fundamental matrix by $\\text{using the initial condition }{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ from $\\text{L1}$ and $c=x(0)$ from $\\text{L5}$ into $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ and substitution from $\\text{L1}\\text{ and }\\text{L5}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391587 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391587 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391587 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391587 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391587 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391587 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391587 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391587 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186391592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391587 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "36126579-e63c-590b-a6f7-f58bde2b64a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186391588 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186391588 #edb/ref 108